    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 79.32 efficiency score. While he faces a slight penalty for the catcher\u2019s arm, his premier batting order slot and favorable matchup against Mahle make him the engine of our offense. Close behind him, **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **Max Muncy** (70.70) offer the most significant upside. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to a prime platoon advantage against Alcantara and a hitter-friendly venue, while **Max Muncy** exploits a soft opposing rotation arm with a similarly strong situational profile. **Seiya Suzuki** rounds out our top-tier tier at 70.60, aided by favorable winds that project to assist his power profile against Canning.\n\nStrategic benching remains critical in our quest for category efficiency. **Travis Bazzana** was our most difficult exclusion, finishing just outside the starting nine with a 44.65 score. While his leadoff position provides inherent value, his platoon disadvantage against Alexander forced him to the bench in favor of higher-floor plays. We also remain cautious with **Jose Caballero**; despite his elite speed, his poor platoon split and bottom-of-the-order assignment suppressed his score to 45.11, putting him at the very edge of our starting threshold. \n\nWe are monitoring the **Zach McKinstry** situation closely, as his sub-50 score reflects the difficulty of facing a sub-4.00 xERA arm, though he is currently slotted in for his speed utility. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on the bench health of **Trevor Story**, who remains on the IL, and we continue to prioritize the development of **Dalton Rushing** and **Cole Young** in our reserve ranks, though they currently fail to meet our efficiency floor for active roster consideration. With **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Henry Bolte** idle, we are relying on our core outfielders to carry the heavy lifting in the stolen base category today.",
